{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# gl(3), L = 2: the two-vacua covectors ⟨Ω_w ⊗ Ω_{w′}| — untwisting with w, w′, z → 1 independently, finite-twist reach, K/S and CG at leading order (Stage D, chain side; 2026-10-11)\n\nImplements `L2-two-vacua-untwist-spec.md` (Tasks 0–6) plus the additional Task 1b (finite-twist reach of the undone covector for the sub-families of Stage B). Built by a sonnet wolfbook-builder, planned and reviewed by the main session. Setting: diagonal frame, new conventions, plain GT generators `JJ` (exact rationals, non-Hermitian, invariant metric `gMet`), L = 2, h = 1/2, θ = (2/7, −3/5) (t = θ₁₂/h = 62/35), exact transfer matrices, 200 digits on the chain, factorised x₀ (never `Inverse` at small ε). This stage is the **chain side** of plan §5: it does not use the bracket formula (Stages B/C).\n\n**One switch.** The only rep-dependent line is `Λ = {2, 1, 0}; nL = 2; ...` in the first code cell. All cells are rep-generic (HW sectors, the vacuum Q degrees and the ψ_Q triple are computed from Λ); each printed-output cell lists the [2,1,0] run and then the [3,1,0] run (the whole notebook was run once per rep by changing that line; the saved file has Λ = {2,1,0}).\n\n**Notebook state.** The cells of this new file were NOT executed natively by VS Code (the file was written as JSON; `wolfbook_runCell` on a freshly created file answers \"NOT executed\"; `wolfbook_newNotebook` / `wolfbook_saveNotebook` were not available). Every code cell was evaluated in the shared kernel K1 from exactly its saved source text (`Get` of a scratch copy of the source, identical to the cell text), and the printed results are stored in the markdown cells below the code cells (\"Printed output of the code cell ...\"). The first cell wipes `Global``.\n\n**Notation.**\n- `ΩD[z,w]` = e₁ᵀρ(n(z,w)), n(z,w) = exp(r₁E₁₂)exp(r₂E₁₃)exp(r₃E₂₃), r_k = r_k(z,w) the diagonal-frame Gauss parameters of the one-site vacuum (`rGauss`; r₁ = (w₁−z₁)/(w₁−z₂), r₂ = (w₁−z₁)(z₁−w₂)(z₂−z₃)/((z₁−z₂)(w₁−z₃)(w₂−z₃)), r₃ = (w₁−z₂)(z₂−w₂)(z₁−z₃)/((z₁−z₂)(w₁−z₃)(z₃−w₂)); they depend on w₁, w₂ only; w₂ = ∞ is the limit). The family is Φ = ΩD[z,w] ⊗ ΩD[z,w′]. In the companion frame ΩC[w] = e₁ᵀρ(exp(E₁₂/w₁)exp(−E₁₃/(w₁w₂))exp((w₁+w₂)/(w₁w₂)E₂₃)) (w₂ = ∞: gaussCov[{1/w₁, 0, 1/w₁}]).\n- n′ := n(z,w) n(z,w′)⁻¹ = [[1,a′,b′],[0,1,c′],[0,0,1]] = exp(a′E₁₂) exp(g′E₁₃) exp(c′E₂₃), **g′ := b′ − a′c′** (the spec's \"b′ − a′c′\", the commutator direction). Exact undo (ρ(n)⊗ρ(n) fixes every HW ket): ⟨ΩD[w] ⊗ ΩD[w′]|h⟩ = ⟨φ_u ⊗ e₁ᵀ|h⟩, **φ_u := e₁ᵀρ(n′)** (no scalar, since e₁ᵀρ(n)e₁ = 1).\n- Chain: HW-limit branches Ψ_B of the twisted chain at z (one per HW ket of Λ⊗Λ, normalised ⟨x₀|Ψ_B⟩ = 1 with x₀ = (e₁ᵀP_phys⁻¹)^{⊗2}), P_HW the G-orthogonal projector onto the HW space of the sector of B, R_C = ⟨Φ|Ψ_B⟩, S = ⟨Φ|P_HWΨ_B⟩, K = R_C − S. A HW state of weight μ has its CG slice at the one-site weight ν = μ − Λ (site 2 = e₁): S = φ_u[ν]·c_B with c_B the slice vector of P_HWΨ_B.\n- Regime: z = 1 + εφ, φ = (1/3, −2/7, 5/11) (control φ′ = (−2/5, 3/8, 7/11)); w = (1+εω₁, 1+εω₂), w′ = (1+εω₁′, 1+εω₂′) (w₃ = 1+5ε/13, w₃′ = 1−4ε/13 drop out of the covector, enter the vacuum Q's only); grid ω₁ ∈ {3/4, −5/3}, ω₂ ∈ {−1/5, 9/7, 5/3}, ω₁′ ∈ {−12/5, 7/2}, ω₂′ ∈ {1/8, −3/4} (24 points, all distinct from the φ_k and from each other); ε ∈ {1,2,4}·10⁻⁶.\n- Families run besides the **main** family: **fixed** (control: w′ = (7/4, −2/5) not untwisted, 6 points), and the Stage B sub-families **inf2** (w₂ = w₂′ = ∞, w₁, w₁′ untwisted; 12 points), **inf1** (w₂′ = ∞ only; 12 points), **common1** (w₁′ = w₁; 12 points).\n\n**Cell map.** 1–2 setup (generators/metric, transfer matrices); 3 group data, vacua, regime; 4 HW kets/projectors; 5 Task 0 checks; 6 Q machinery, eigenstates, HW-limit branches; 7 Task 1; 8 Task 1b; 9 Task 2; 10 Task 3; 11 Task 4; 12 Task 5; final markdown = Task 6.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
