   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 0 result: setup, frame tie, exact undo (cells 1–6; two runs, `Λ` changed in the first code cell)\n\n| check (all exact unless stated) | [2,1,0] (dim 8, 64 states) | [3,1,0] (dim 15, 225 states) |\n|---|---|---|\n| gl(3) relations; G unique, positive, invariant; nilpotency E_ij^(λ₁−λ₃+1) = 0 | True | True |\n| quantum determinant dev (200 digits); [t₁,t₂] dev | 2.9e-200; 4.0e-194 | 5.8e-200; 1.4e-193 |\n| expN = MatrixExp on root generators; factorised x₀ = x₀ from `Inverse` (exact); n(z,w) 3×3 = product of exponentials; ΩD = full-matrix exponentials; ρ multiplicative | True | True |\n| HW kets / HW sectors (computed from the raising operators; multiplicities) | 6 / 5 (1,1,1,2,1) | 10 / 8 (1,1,1,2,1,2,1,1) |\n| slice weights ν = μ−Λ and dims | (2,1,0)₁ (2,0,1)₁ (1,2,0)₁ (1,1,1)₂ (0,1,2)₁ | (3,1,0)₁ (3,0,1)₁ (2,2,0)₁ (2,1,1)₂ (1,3,0)₁ (1,2,1)₂ (1,1,2)₂ (0,2,2)₁ |\n| G-orthogonal projectors per HW sector: idempotent, fix the HW kets, G-orthogonal residual | True | True |\n| **(a) frame tie** at 6 rational points (2 with w₂ = ∞, 1 regime point ε = 1e-6): ΩC[w] ∥ ΩD[z,w]·P_phys(z), scalar = κ | True (6/6) | True (6/6) |\n| **(b) exact undo** ⟨ΩD[w]⊗ΩD[w′]\\|h⟩ = ⟨e₁ρ(n(w)n(w′)⁻¹)⊗e₁\\|h⟩ on all HW kets at 7 points (2 with w₂ = ∞, 2 regime points); naive e₁⊗e₁ pairing differs (control) | True (7/7); controls differ | True (7/7); controls differ |\n| **(c)** ΩD[w]⊗ΩD[w] left eigen-covector of t_a(2/9), a = 1,2,3, with the bra twist G′(w) = P_aux G(w) P_aux⁻¹; control twist diag(w) | True,True,True; control False,False,True | True,True,True; control False,False,True |\n| continuity of ΩD at w₂ = 10¹⁰, 10³⁰ vs w₂ = ∞ (max abs diff) | 2.2e-10, 2.2e-30 | 9.5e-10, 9.5e-30 |\n| states / HW-limit branches at ε = 1e-6; top branch = e₁⊗e₁ (rel dev); raising residual of branches vs the rest; ‖P_HWΨ_B‖/‖Ψ_B‖ ≥ | 21 / 6; < 1e-191; ≤ 4.1e-7 vs ≥ 1.3; 1 − 1.7e-14 | 56 / 10; < 1e-191; ≤ 1.0e-6 vs ≥ 1.4; 1 − 8.2e-14 |\n| exact Baxter residual of all dual Q's (stored numbers); Precision of ψ | 1.1e-147; 162 | 2.4e-140; 155 |\n| time (s): cells 1–6 | 0.05, 0.26, 0.09, 0.03, 0.16, 1.5 | 0.07, 1.6, 0.22, 0.12, 0.86, 5.2 |\n\n**Two differences from the spec's wording** (both exact, found in this notebook). (1) The frame tie holds **up to a scalar**: ΩC[w] = ΩD[z,w]·P_phys(z)/κ(z,w) with κ = ⟨e₁\\|ρ(n P)\\|e₁⟩ = Π_k Δ_k(n(z,w)·P₃(z))^{λ_k−λ_{k+1}} (Δ_k leading principal minors of the 3×3 matrix; P₃ the defining-rep image of P_phys), because ΩC is normalised to first component 1 and ΩD·P_phys is not; the ratio is parallel at every point, also for w₂ = ∞. (2) The bra twist of which Ω_w⊗Ω_w is the eigen-covector, written in the diagonal frame, is G′(w) = P_aux G(w) P_aux⁻¹ (the companion matrix G(w) with eigenvalues w conjugated into the diagonal frame), **not** diag(w): with diag(w) the eigen-test fails for t₁, t₂ (control above).",
