   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 1 result: the undone unipotent n′ = n(z,w) n(z,w′)⁻¹, symbolic in ε (cell 7; exact, rep-independent: the same 3×3 data for both reps)\n\n**All three Gauss parameters are O(1) at ε = 0** (orders 0, 0, 0 for a′, c′, g′ = b′−a′c′; exact `Together`/exponent count). Closed forms of the ε = 0 values (`Factor`, in φ = (f₁,f₂,f₃), ω = (o₁,o₂), ω′ = (p₁,p₂)):\n\n- **a′₀ = (φ₁−φ₂)(ω₁−ω₁′) / ((ω₁−φ₂)(ω₁′−φ₂))** (= r₁⁰(ω) − r₁⁰(ω′), r₁⁰(ω) = (ω₁−φ₁)/(ω₁−φ₂); depends on ω₁, ω₁′ only);\n- **g′₀ = (b′−a′c′)₀ = (φ₁−φ₃)(φ₂−φ₃)(ω₁−ω₁′)(ω₂−ω₁′) / ((φ₃−ω₁)(φ₃−ω₂)(φ₃−ω₁′)(ω₁′−φ₂))** (depends on ω₁, ω₂, ω₁′; **not** on ω₂′);\n- **c′₀ = (φ₁−φ₃)(φ₂−φ₃) N / ((φ₁−φ₂)(φ₃−ω₁)(φ₃−ω₂)(φ₃−ω₁′)(φ₃−ω₂′))**, N = φ₂φ₃(ω₁+ω₂−ω₁′−ω₂′) − (φ₂+φ₃)(ω₁ω₂−ω₁′ω₂′) + ω₁ω₂(ω₁′+ω₂′) − ω₁′ω₂′(ω₁+ω₂) (= r₃⁰(ω) − r₃⁰(ω′), r₃⁰(ω) = (ω₁−φ₂)(φ₂−ω₂)(φ₁−φ₃)/((φ₁−φ₂)(ω₁−φ₃)(φ₃−ω₂)); depends on all four).\n\n**Rank of the map (ω₁, ω₂, ω₁′, ω₂′) ↦ (a′₀, c′₀, g′₀): 3** (Jacobian rank 3 at three generic rational points, one with φ′); the fibre is one-dimensional.\n\n**Exact structure (checked symbolically):** n(w) = [[1,a,b],[0,1,c],[0,0,1]] with a = r₁, **b = r₂ + r₁r₃ = (w₁−z₁)/(w₁−z₃) independent of w₂**, c = r₃. Hence a′ = a − a_{w′}, c′ = c − c_{w′} and **g′ = (b − b_{w′}) − (a − a_{w′}) c**: the commutator direction depends on w′ only through w₁′ (through a_{w′}, b_{w′}) and on w only through w₁, w₂.\n\n**Controls** (leading orders of (a′, c′, g′); leading coefficients in the printed output):\n\n| control | result |\n|---|---|\n| (i) w′ = w exactly | n′ = 1 (all three vanish identically) |\n| (ii-a) the old regime's pinning: w₂′ = y₀(1+εω₂′), y₀ = (t−1)/(t−2) = −27/8 at t = 62/35, w₁′ = 1+εω₁′ | **orders (0,0,0)**: all three stay O(1); g′₀ is the same function as in the main family (independent of ω₂′); only c′₀ changes (it loses ω₂′) |\n| (ii-b) w₂′ = 7/4 fixed, w₁′ untwisted | orders (0,0,0), same a′₀, g′₀ |\n| (ii-c) w′ = (7/4, −2/5) fixed (no w′ untwisting at all) | orders (0,0,0); a′₀ = (φ₁−φ₂)/(φ₂−ω₁), g′₀ = −(φ₁−φ₃)(φ₂−φ₃)/((φ₃−ω₁)(φ₃−ω₂)), c′₀ = (φ₁−φ₃)(φ₂−φ₃)(φ₂+φ₃−ω₁−ω₂)/((φ₁−φ₂)(φ₃−ω₁)(φ₃−ω₂)): the map (ω₁,ω₂) ↦ (a′₀,c′₀,g′₀) has rank 2 |\n| (iii) common w₁′ = w₁ (w₂′ = 1+εω₂′) | **a′ ≡ 0 and g′ ≡ 0 exactly**, c′₀ = (φ₁−φ₃)(φ₂−φ₃)(φ₂−ω₁)(ω₂−ω₂′)/((φ₁−φ₂)(φ₃−ω₁)(φ₃−ω₂)(φ₃−ω₂′)): n′ = exp(c′E₂₃), only the E₂₃ direction survives (the localising-span result) |\n| (iv) common w₂′ = w₂, w₁′ untwisted | orders (0,0,0); c′₀ ∝ (ω₁−ω₁′)(φ₂−ω₂) |\n\n**Surprise (spec expectation not realised).** The spec expected b′−a′c′ to drop an order when w₂′ is pinned at an O(1) value (the old det₆×det₂ degeneration). It does not: the old family had the second site's vacuum slaved to a resolvent of the first (y pinned, n′ = Δ⁻¹nΔn⁻¹, g′ = a′c′(z₂−w₂)/(y−z₂) with a pinned denominator, per the earlier gl(3)/gl(4) notebooks), whereas here the two vacua are independent and g′ = (b−b_{w′}) − (a−a_{w′})c has no ω₂′ dependence at all and no pinned denominator. The only way to lose a direction is w₁′ = w₁ (control iii).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
