  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 2 result: ε-structure of φ_u(ε) = e₁ᵀρ(n′(ε)) per weight (cell 9; exact, symbolic ε, 24 grid points; φ and φ′)\n\nPer site-1 weight of V: leading ε-order of the components (minimum and maximum over the 24 points), rank of the ε⁰ coefficient vectors over the grid, rank including the ε¹ coefficients.\n\n| family (points) | weights at order ε⁰ (min = max order over the grid) | rank of ε⁰ coefficients | rank incl. ε¹ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **main** (24), φ and φ′ (identical tables) | **all 7 [2,1,0] / all 12 [3,1,0]** | **= multiplicity: 1 on the 1-dim weights, 2 on (1,1,1) [2,1,0]; 2 on (2,1,1), (1,2,1), (1,1,2) [3,1,0]** | same (nothing new at ε¹: the ε⁰ data are already complete) |\n| control: w′ = (7/4, −2/5) fixed (6 points) | all weights at ε⁰ | full (= multiplicity) | same |\n| extra inf2: w₂ = w₂′ = ∞ (12 points) | all weights at ε⁰ | full | same |\n| extra inf1: w₂′ = ∞ only (12 points) | all weights at ε⁰ | full | same |\n| extra common1: w₁′ = w₁ (12 points) | only (2,1,0), (2,0,1) [(3,1,0), (3,0,1)]; all other weights **identically zero** (order ∞) | 1 on these two, 0 elsewhere | same |\n\n**Adjoint, main family, weight by weight (identical for φ′):**\n\n| weight | dim | min order | max order | rank ε⁰ | rank ε⁰+ε¹ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (0,1,2) | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n| (0,2,1) | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n| (1,0,2) | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n| (1,1,1) | 2 | 0 | 0 | 2 | 2 |\n| (1,2,0) | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n| (2,0,1) | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n| (2,1,0) | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n\n(the [3,1,0] table is the same statement for 12 weights; see the printed output). **Expectation confirmed: every weight at ε⁰ with rank = multiplicity.** In contrast the old det₆×det₂ family had the depth table ε⁰, ε¹, ε¹, ε², ε³, ε³, ε⁴ (adjoint), three orders for [3,1,0].\n\n**Control (not realised as the spec expected).** The spec expected the w′ = fixed control to reproduce a depth table. It does not: with w′ = (7/4, −2/5) fixed the undone unipotent is n(z,w) n₁⁻¹ with n₁ the finite z → (1,1,1) limit of n(z,w′), which is a generic unipotent, so all three Gauss parameters and hence every weight are O(1) (Task 1 (ii-c)). The map (ω₁,ω₂) ↦ (a′₀,c′₀,g′₀) then has rank 2 only, but the per-weight ranks are still full over the 6 points, and Task 3/4 show K/S = O(ε) and all CG data also for this control. Untwisting w′ is therefore **not** needed for cleanliness of this family; what matters is only that w₁′ ≠ w₁ (g′ = (b−b_{w′}) − (a−a_{w′})c vanishes iff w₁′ = w₁ or c is tuned).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 3. Chain side: signal vs contamination",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 3. Chain side: signal vs contamination. For a family point: Phi = OmegaD[z,w] (x) OmegaD[z,w'] (200 digits), R_C = <Phi|Psi_B> (<x0|Psi_B> = 1 by branchesAt), S = <Phi|P_HW Psi_B> (G-orthogonal projector onto the HW space of the sector of B), K = R_C - S. Exact undo, checked numerically: S = <phi_u (x) e1|P_HW Psi_B>. epsilon-exponents are log2 ratios between consecutive eps (ratio 2): S ~ eps^e means the ratio of S(2e)/S(e) is 2^e. The HW-limit branches depend on eps only (not on the grid point), so they are built once per (eps, phi). *)\nnb = Length[hwList];\nchainData[ie_, ph_] := chainData[ie, ph] = Module[{zz = 1 + epsL[[ie]] ph, B}, B = branchesAt[zz];\n  Table[With[{b = brOf[B, hwList[[ib, 1]], hwList[[ib, 2]]]}, <|\"psi\" -> b[\"psi\"], \"ph\" -> PHWc[b[\"mu\"]][b[\"psi\"]], \"normG\" -> gNorm[b[\"psi\"]], \"hwFrac\" -> b[\"hwFrac\"]|>], {ib, nb}]];\nt3Point[fam_, ph_, ie_, pt_] := Module[{eps = epsL[[ie]], zz = 1 + epsL[[ie]] ph, ws, cd = chainData[ie, ph], Phi, phe},\n  ws = fam[\"wOf\"][eps, pt[[1]], pt[[2]]];\n  Phi = kron[N[ΩD[zz, ws[[1]]], pr], N[ΩD[zz, ws[[2]]], pr]]; phe = kron[N[phiUof[zz, ws[[1]], ws[[2]]], pr], e1];\n  Table[With[{d = cd[[ib]]}, With[{RC = Phi . d[\"psi\"], S = Phi . d[\"ph\"], und = phe . d[\"ph\"]}, <|\"RC\" -> RC, \"S\" -> S, \"K\" -> RC - S, \"undo\" -> If[S == 0, 0, Abs[(S - und)/S]]|>]], {ib, nb}]];\nt3Run[fam_, ph_, ies_] := Table[t3Point[fam, ph, ie, pt], {ie, ies}, {pt, fam[\"pts\"]}];\nexpo2[a_, b_] := If[a == 0 || b == 0, Indeterminate, N[Log[Abs[b/a]]/Log[2], 6]];\n(* timing of one point, one eps *)\n{tT3one, t3one} = AbsoluteTiming[t3Point[famMain, phiP, 1, famMain[\"pts\"][[1]]]];\nT3 = <||>;\n{tMain, T3[\"main\"]} = AbsoluteTiming[t3Run[famMain, phiP, {1, 2, 3}]];\n{tFix, T3[\"fixed\"]} = AbsoluteTiming[t3Run[famFixed, phiP, {1, 2, 3}]];\n{tInf2, T3[\"inf2\"]} = AbsoluteTiming[t3Run[famInf2, phiP, {1, 2, 3}]];\n{tInf1, T3[\"inf1\"]} = AbsoluteTiming[t3Run[famInf1, phiP, {1, 2, 3}]];\n{tCom, T3[\"common1\"]} = AbsoluteTiming[t3Run[famCommon1, phiP, {1, 2, 3}]];\n{tMainC, T3[\"mainC\"]} = AbsoluteTiming[t3Run[famMain, phiC, {1}]];\n(* per-branch summary: exponent range of S and of K over the points (pairs eps1->eps2, eps2->eps3), max |K/S| at each eps, scaling of max|K/S| (doubles with eps iff K/S = O(eps)); a branch is \"read\" if |S| > 1e-100 |R_C| at some point (the family reaches its slice weight) *)\nfmtE[x_] := If[x == 0, \"0 (acc \" <> ToString[Round[Accuracy[x]]] <> \")\", With[{e = Floor[Log10[Abs[x]]]}, ToString[Round[x/10^e, 0.01]] <> \"e\" <> ToString[e]]];\nbranchRead[Tf_, ib_] := Max[Table[Abs[Tf[[1, ip, ib, \"S\"]]/Tf[[1, ip, ib, \"RC\"]]], {ip, Length[Tf[[1]]]}]] > 10^-100;\nksTab[Tf_, nEps_] := Table[If[! branchRead[Tf, ib], {hwList[[ib, 1]], hwList[[ib, 2]], \"not read\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}, Module[{np = Length[Tf[[1]]], S, K, eS, eK, mx, flatK0},\n   S = Table[Tf[[ie, ip, ib, \"S\"]], {ie, nEps}, {ip, np}]; K = Table[Tf[[ie, ip, ib, \"K\"]], {ie, nEps}, {ip, np}];\n   mx = Table[Max[Abs[K[[ie]]/S[[ie]]]], {ie, nEps}]; flatK0 = Max[mx] < 10^-120;\n   eS = If[nEps > 1, Table[expo2[S[[ie, ip]], S[[ie + 1, ip]]], {ie, nEps - 1}, {ip, np}], {{0}}];\n   eK = If[flatK0 || nEps < 2, {{0}}, Table[expo2[K[[ie, ip]], K[[ie + 1, ip]]], {ie, nEps - 1}, {ip, np}]];\n   {hwList[[ib, 1]], hwList[[ib, 2]], If[nEps > 1, ToString[NumberForm[#, {5, 3}] & /@ MinMax[Flatten[eS]]], \"-\"], If[flatK0, \"K=0\", If[nEps > 1, ToString[NumberForm[#, {5, 3}] & /@ MinMax[Flatten[eK]]], \"-\"]], If[flatK0, \"0\", StringRiffle[fmtE /@ mx, \", \"]], If[nEps >= 3 && ! flatK0, ToString[N[mx[[2]]/mx[[1]], 4]] <> \", \" <> ToString[N[mx[[3]]/mx[[2]], 4]], \"-\"], fmtE[Max[Table[Tf[[ie, ip, ib, \"undo\"]], {ie, nEps}, {ip, np}]]]}]], {ib, nb}];\nfamKeys = {\"main\", \"fixed\", \"inf2\", \"inf1\", \"common1\", \"mainC\"};\nfamNEps = <|\"main\" -> 3, \"fixed\" -> 3, \"inf2\" -> 3, \"inf1\" -> 3, \"common1\" -> 3, \"mainC\" -> 1|>;\nfamLab = <|\"main\" -> \"MAIN family (24 points, phi)\", \"fixed\" -> \"CONTROL w' fixed = (7/4, -2/5) (6 points)\", \"inf2\" -> \"EXTRA w2 = w2' = Infinity (12 points)\", \"inf1\" -> \"EXTRA w2' = Infinity only (12 points)\", \"common1\" -> \"EXTRA common w1' = w1 (12 points)\", \"mainC\" -> \"MAIN family with phi' (24 points, eps = 1e-6 only)\"|>;\nksAll = Association[Table[k -> ksTab[T3[k], famNEps[k]], {k, famKeys}]];\nchecks[\"T3 K/S = O(eps) for every branch of the main family (max|K/S| doubles with eps: ratios in [1.9, 2.1])\"] = And @@ Table[r[[6]] === \"-\" || (And @@ (1.9 < ToExpression[#] < 2.1 & /@ StringSplit[r[[6]], \", \"])), {r, ksAll[\"main\"]}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"family\", \"mu\", \"copy\", \"S: eps-exp range\", \"K: eps-exp range\", \"max |K/S| at eps = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6\", \"ratios of max|K/S| (O(eps): 2, 2)\", \"max undo rel dev\"}}, Flatten[Table[Join[{{famLab[k], \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}, Table[{\"\", r[[1]], r[[2]], r[[3]], r[[4]], r[[5]], r[[6]], r[[7]]}, {r, ksAll[k]}]], {k, famKeys}], 1], {{\"main family: K/S = O(eps) for every branch\", ToString[checks[\"T3 K/S = O(eps) for every branch of the main family (max|K/S| doubles with eps: ratios in [1.9, 2.1])\"]], \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"time (s): one point, main (72 pts), fixed, inf2, inf1, common1, phi'\", ToString[N[{tT3one, tMain, tFix, tInf2, tInf1, tCom, tMainC}, 3], InputForm], \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "*Printed output of the code cell `c10_t3_chain` (evaluated in the shared kernel from exactly the saved source; not a native notebook output).*\n\n**[2,1,0] run** (rows of the printed `Grid`, InputForm; first entry = cell id, second = time in s):\n\n```\n{\"c10_t3_chain\", 4.97, {{\"family\", \"mu\", \"copy\", \"S: eps-exp range\", \"K: eps-exp range\", \"max |K/S| at eps = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6\", \"ratios of max|K/S| (O(eps): 2, 2)\", \"max undo rel dev\"}, \n  {\"MAIN family (24 points, phi)\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"\", {4, 2, 0}, 1, \"{-2.000, -2.000}\", \"K=0\", \"0\", \"-\", \"0 (acc 192)\"}, \n  {\"\", {4, 1, 1}, 1, \"{-3.000, -3.000}\", \"{-2.000, -2.000}\", \"4.25e-7, 8.5e-7, 1.7e-6\", \"2.000, 2.000\", \"0 (acc 184)\"}, \n  {\"\", {3, 3, 0}, 1, \"{-3.000, -3.000}\", \"{-2.000, -2.000}\", \"2.1e-6, 4.21e-6, 8.42e-6\", \"2.000, 2.000\", \"0 (acc 184)\"}, \n  {\"\", {3, 2, 1}, 1, \"{-4.000, -4.000}\", \"{-3.000, -3.000}\", \"1.5e-5, 3.01e-5, 6.01e-5\", \"2.000, 2.000\", \"0 (acc 173)\"}, \n  {\"\", {3, 2, 1}, 2, \"{-4.000, -4.000}\", \"{-3.000, -3.000}\", \"8.05e-6, 1.61e-5, 3.22e-5\", \"2.000, 2.000\", \"0 (acc 174)\"}, \n  {\"\", {2, 2, 2}, 1, \"{-6.000, -6.000}\", \"{-5.000, -5.000}\", \"2.57e-6, 5.14e-6, 1.03e-5\", \"2.000, 2.000\", \"0 (acc 157)\"}, {\"CONTROL w' fixed = (7/4, -2/5) (6 points)\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}, \n  {\"\", {4, 2, 0}, 1, \"{-2.000, -2.000}\", \"K=0\", \"0\", \"-\", \"0 (acc 192)\"}, {\"\", {4, 1, 1}, 1, \"{-3.000, -3.000}\", \"{-2.000, -2.000}\", \"6.02e-6, 1.2e-5, 2.41e-5\", \"2.000, 2.000\", \"0 (acc 183)\"}, \n  {\"\", {3, 3, 0}, 1, \"{-3.000, -3.000}\", \"{-2.000, -2.000}\", \"6.52e-7, 1.3e-6, 2.61e-6\", \"2.000, 2.000\", \"0 (acc 184)\"}, \n  {\"\", {3, 2, 1}, 1, \"{-4.000, -4.000}\", \"{-3.000, -3.000}\", \"6.03e-7, 1.21e-6, 2.41e-6\", \"2.000, 2.000\", \"0 (acc 174)\"}, \n  {\"\", {3, 2, 1}, 2, \"{-4.000, -4.000}\", \"{-3.000, -3.000}\", \"1.36e-6, 2.72e-6, 5.45e-6\", \"2.00