   "value": "### Task 4 result: CG data at leading order from the overlap alone (cell 11)\n\n1-dim slices: C := R_C/φ_u(0)[slice] (φ_u(0) = exact ε⁰ coefficient vector, verified equal to e₁ᵀρ(exp(a′₀E₁₂)exp(g′₀E₁₃)exp(c′₀E₂₃)) with the Task 1 closed forms at all 24 points), error = max over the grid of |C/c_B − 1| with c_B the chain slice, spread = max over the grid of |C/mean − 1|. 2-dim slices: the 2×2 system from two grid points with independent φ_u(0)[slice] (pairs (k, k+n/2) of the n grid points: 12 pairs for the main grid), componentwise errors/spreads over the pairs. Errors and spreads are O(ε) (column \"err(4e-6)/err(1e-6)\" = 4.00 everywhere). Richardson (ε = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6) on f = C·ε^p, p = −(ε-exponent of the slice): the chain limit and the limit of the overlap-extracted data agree to the stated number (column \"agreement\": `< 1e-N` means identical to the accuracy bound of the working precision — as for the 1-dim slices of the first irreps in the earlier det₆×det₂ notebook — otherwise 1e-16 … 1e-20, the O(ε³) remainder after the second-order Richardson).\n\n**All CG data are read at leading order from the overlap: 6 of 6 HW data of adj⊗adj (singlet and both octets with both components) and 10 of 10 of [3,1,0] (including [4,4,0], [4,3,1]×2, [4,2,2], [3,3,2]), for the main family, the fixed-w′ control, and the sub-families inf2 and inf1.** (common1 reads only the first two irreps, see Task 3.)\n\n**Reference numbers (chain slice normalisation ⟨x₀|Ψ⟩ = 1, so the chain limits are family-independent and must coincide with the earlier notebooks):** adjoint [4,1,1] 46.67453891 ✓, [3,3,0] 10.92853892 ✓, singlet −5118.538314 ✓, octets (u+u′)·C = C₁+3C₂: 184.3305612 ✓ and −238.5587523 ✓ (octet mixing R = u·C/((u+u′)·C) from the chain vectors: −1.6944 and 1.0956, the earlier −1.694, 1.096 ✓); [3,1,0] [6,1,1] 46.6745 ✓, [5,3,0] −36.8838 ✓, [5,2,1] (u′·C = 2C₁+8C₂) −1325.402367 ✓ and −334.3316172 ✓ (the earlier −1325.40…, −334.33…). New numbers for [3,1,0] (chain 