  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 5 result: det₆-type data of the family at small ε (cell 12; for the Stage C / Q-side task)\n\nOne grid point (ω, ω′) = ((3/4, −1/5), (−12/5, 1/8)), ε = 1e-6 (the exponents from ε = 1e-6 → 2e-6), w₃ = 1+5ε/13, w₃′ = 1−4ε/13.\n\n- **Vacuum direct Q's** of the bra twists w and w′: degrees (0,2,4) [2,1,0] / (0,4,6) [3,1,0], exact Baxter residuals 4.5e-191, 2.5e-190 / 7.4e-190, 9.2e-190. **Dual Q's** of all states of the HW sectors: degrees = μ_j (all 21 / 56 states), residual 1.1e-147 / 2.4e-140.\n- **Diagonal overlaps = det₆:** ⟨Ω_w⊗Ω_w|Ψ⟩ = c_w·det₆[B,F_vac(w)]/Ψ_Q and the same for w′ with a constant c_{w′}, state-independent over all 21 resp. 56 states of the HW sectors: max relative deviation 3.2e-116, 1.8e-117 [2,1,0]; 6.4e-77, 1.5e-85 [3,1,0] (limited by the ~100-digit precision of the Q-determinants). The constants (state-independent, not needed here): c_w ≈ 9.80e69 + 2.61e70 i, c_{w′} ≈ 1.51e65 + 4.02e65 i [2,1,0]; c_w ≈ 1.14e96 + 3.03e96 i, c_{w′} ≈ 4.50e88 + 1.20e89 i [3,1,0].\n- **The four overlaps** on the HW-limit branches (the mixed ones are the Q-number targets of Stage C: they are NOT det₆):\n\n**[2,1,0], main family, grid point (om, om') = ((3/4,-1/5), (-12/5,1/8)), eps = 1e-6 (mantissa e exponent; exponents from eps = 1e-6 -> 2e-6):**\n\n| irrep | copy | <w w\\|Psi> | <w' w'\\|Psi> | <w w'\\|Psi> | <w' w\\|Psi> | eps-exponents (ww, pp, wp, pw) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [4,2,0] | 1 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | -2, -2, -2, -2 |\n| [4,1,1] | 1 | -1.198e12 | -2.409e12 | -4.241e18 | 4.241e18 | -2, -2, -3, -3 |\n| [3,3,0] | 1 | 1.05e12 | 3.374e12 | -9.732e18 | 9.732e18 | -2, -2, -3, -3 |\n| [3,2,1] | 1 | 4.367e18 | 5.889e18 | -1.515e26 | 2.066e26 | -3, -3, -4, -4 |\n| [3,2,1] | 2 | -1.153e19 | -1.555e19 | -1.585e26 | 1.411e26 | -3, -3, -4, -4 |\n| [2,2,2] | 1 | -4.533e25 | -8.244e25 | 5.02e39 | 5.02e39 | -4, -4, -6, -6 |\n\n**[2,1,0], extra sub-family w2 = w2' = Infinity, (om1, om1') = (3/4, -12/5), eps = 1e-6:**\n\n| irrep | copy | <w w\\|Psi> | <w' w'\\|Psi> | <w w'\\|Psi> | <w' w\\|Psi> | eps-exponents (ww, pp, wp, pw) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [4,2,0] | 1 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | -2, -2, -2, -2 |\n| [4,1,1] | 1 | 9.147e12 | 1.933e12 | -2.527e19 | 2.527e19 | -2, -2, -3, -3 |\n| [3,3,0] | 1 | 1.05e12 | 3.374e12 | -9.732e18 | 9.732e18 | -2, -2, -3, -3 |\n| [3,2,1] | 1 | 3.68e12 | 2.499e12 | 1.384e26 | 1.899e26 | -2, -2, -4, -4 |\n| [3,2,1] | 2 | 3.68e12 | 2.499e12 | -7.358e25 | -3.044e25 | -2, -2, -4, -4 |\n| [2,2,2] | 1 | 5.19e12 | 2.393e12 | -7.876e38 | -7.876e38 | -2, -2, -6, -6 |\n\n**[3,1,0], main family, grid point (om, om') = ((3/4,-1/5), (-12/5,1/8)), eps = 1e-6 (mantissa e exponent; exponents from eps = 1e-6 -> 2e-6):**\n\n| irrep | copy | <w w\\|Psi> | <w' w'\\|Psi> | <w w'\\|Psi> | <w' w\\|Psi> | eps-exponents (ww, pp, wp, pw) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [6,2,0] | 1 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | -2, -2, -2, -2 |\n| [6,1,1] | 1 | -1.198e12 | -2.409e12 | -4.241e18 | 4.241e18 | -2, -2, -3, -3 |\n| [5,3,0] | 1 | 1.05e12 | 3.374e12 | 6.569e19 | -6.569e19 | -2, -2, -3, -3 |\n| [5,2,1] | 1 | 3.518e18 | 4.745e18 | 5.228e26 | -8.329e26 | -3, -3, -4, -4 |\n| [5,2,1] | 2 | -2.289e19 | -3.087e19 | -2.415e26 | 2.2e26 | -3, -3, -4, -4 |\n| [4,4,0] | 1 | 4.223e11 | 4.361e12 | -1.837e26 | -1.837e26 | -2, -2, -4, -4 |\n| [4,3,1] | 1 | 3.21e18 | 1.391e19 | -6.569e33 | -8.23e33 | -3, -3, -5, -5 |\n| [4,3,1] | 2 | -6.094e18 | -2.641e19 | -2.607e33 | -2.316e33 | -3, -3, -5, -5 |\n| [4,2,2] | 1 | -4.719e25 | -8.582e25 | -2.431e40 | -2.431e40 | -4, -4, -6, -6 |\n| [3,3,2] | 1 | -3.419e25 | -1.998e26 | 1.089e47 | -1.089e47 | -4, -4, -7, -7 |\n\n**[3,1,0], extra sub-family w2 = w2' = Infinity, (om1, om1') = (3/4, -12/5), eps = 1e-6:**\n\n| irrep | copy | <w w\\|Psi> | <w' w'\\|Psi> | <w w'\\|Psi> | <w' w\\|Psi> | eps-exponents (ww, pp, wp, pw) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [6,2,0] | 1 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | 2.609e12 | -2, -2, -2, -2 |\n| [6,1,1] | 1 | 9.147e12 | 1.933e12 | -2.527e19 | 2.527e19 | -2, -2, -3, -3 |\n| [5,3,0] | 1 | 1.05e12 | 3.374e12 | 6.569e19 | -6.569e19 | -2, -2, -3, -3 |\n| [5,2,1] | 1 | 3.68e12 | 2.499e12 | -8.264e26 | -1.022e27 | -2, -2, -4, -4 |\n| [5,2,1] | 2 | 3.68e12 | 2.499e12 | -9.737e25 | -3.092e25 | -2, -2, -4, -4 |\n| [4,4,0] | 1 | 4.223e11 | 4.361e12 | -1.837e26 | -1.837e26 | -2, -2, -4, -4 |\n| [4,3,1] | 1 | 1.48e12 | 3.23e12 | 3.884e33 | -6.015e33 | -2, -2, -5, -5 |\n| [4,3,1] | 2 | 1.48e12 | 3.23e12 | -1.222e33 | 5.132e32 | -2, -2, -5, -5 |\n| [4,2,2] | 1 | 5.19e12 | 2.393e12 | 3.814e39 | 3.814e39 | -2, -2, -6, -6 |\n| [3,3,2] | 1 | 2.088e12 | 3.093e12 | -1.708e46 | 1.708e46 | -2, -2, -7, -7 |\n\n**Observations.** (1) The diagonal overlaps scale like ε⁻² (top, 1-dim slices of the first irreps) … ε⁻⁴ ([2,2,2]/[4,2,2]/[3,3,2]), i.e. with the norm of Ψ_B, while the mixed overlaps carry zero (top) to three extra powers of ε⁻¹ (exponent −2 for the top, −3 for [4,1,1]/[3,3,0]/[6,1,1]/[5,3,0], −4 for the octets and [4,4,0], −5 for [4,3,1], −6 for [2,2,2]/[4,2,2], −7 for [3,3,2]): the mixed overlap is the one that carries the CG slice (its exponent equals that of the slice, cf. Task 3's S exponents). (2) For the 1-dim slices ⟨Ω_w⊗Ω_{w′}|Ψ⟩ = ± ⟨Ω_{w′}⊗Ω_w|Ψ⟩ to the leading digits (the sign is the exchange parity of the irrep: − for [4,1,1], [3,3,0], [6,1,1], [5,3,0], [3,3,2]; + for the top, [2,2,2], [4,4,0], [4,2,2]); for the 2-dim slices with two copies (octets, [5,2,1], [4,3,1]) the two mixed overlaps differ ([4,2,2], a 2-dim slice with one copy, is symmetric). (3) For the sub-family w₂ = w₂′ = ∞ the exponents are the same (−2 for the diagonal ones: the ∞-vacua are top-heavy) and the mixed overlaps again carry the slice exponents.",
