   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### two vacua Ω_w⊗Ω_{w′}: untwist result (2026-10-11)\n\nChain side of plan §5, gl(3), L = 2, [2,1,0] and [3,1,0]; diagonal frame; z = 1+εφ, w = 1+εω, w′ = 1+εω′ (24-point grid), ε = 1,2,4·10⁻⁶, 200 digits. Evidence: [exact] symbolic/rational; [numeric] 200-digit chain.\n\n**1. The undone unipotent [exact, rep-independent] (Task 1).** n′ = n(z,w)n(z,w′)⁻¹ = exp(a′E₁₂)exp(g′E₁₃)exp(c′E₂₃), g′ = b′−a′c′. All three are O(1) at ε = 0:\n- a′₀ = (φ₁−φ₂)(ω₁−ω₁′)/((ω₁−φ₂)(ω₁′−φ₂)),\n- g′₀ = (φ₁−φ₃)(φ₂−φ₃)(ω₁−ω₁′)(ω₂−ω₁′)/((φ₃−ω₁)(φ₃−ω₂)(φ₃−ω₁′)(ω₁′−φ₂)),\n- c′₀ = r₃⁰(ω) − r₃⁰(ω′), r₃⁰(ω) = (ω₁−φ₂)(φ₂−ω₂)(φ₁−φ₃)/((φ₁−φ₂)(ω₁−φ₃)(φ₃−ω₂)) (long closed form in Task 1);\n- the map (ω₁,ω₂,ω₁′,ω₂′) ↦ (a′₀,c′₀,g′₀) has **rank 3** (a′₀(ω₁,ω₁′), g′₀(ω₁,ω₂,ω₁′), c′₀(all four)); structure: b = r₂+r₁r₃ = (w₁−z₁)/(w₁−z₃) is w₂-independent, g′ = (b−b_{w′}) − (a−a_{w′})c.\n- Controls: w′ = w gives n′ = 1; **common w₁′ = w₁: a′ ≡ g′ ≡ 0 exactly, n′ = exp(c′E₂₃)**; pinning w₂′ at an O(1) value (y₀ = (t−1)/(t−2), or 7/4), or fixing w′ completely, does **not** make g′ drop an order (spec expectation not realised): all three stay O(1).\n\n**2. Reach [exact].** Finite twist (Task 1b): generic (w,w′), w₂′ = ∞ only, common w₂′ = w₂ and **w₂ = w₂′ = ∞ with w₁′ ≠ w₁** all reach every weight of V (8/8, 15/15) with full rank (2 on the double weights) and read all slice weights: CG-complete. **Common w₁′ = w₁ reads two weights only (top + [4,1,1] resp. [6,1,1]), not CG-complete; w₂ = w₂′ = ∞ with w₁′ = w₁ (global rotation) reads the top weight only.** In the regime (Task 2): the main family has every weight at order ε⁰ with rank = multiplicity (2 on (1,1,1); 2 on (2,1,1), (1,2,1), (1,1,2)), identical for φ′; the same holds for the control w′ fixed, inf2 and inf1; common1 has only the two weights.\n\n**3. K/S [numeric].** The decisive expectation **K/S = O(ε) for every branch holds**, for [2,1,0] (all 6, incl. singlet and both octets) and [3,1,0] (all 10, incl. [4,4,0], [4,3,1]×2, [4,2,2], [3,3,2]); max|K/S| doubles with ε in every branch (ratios 2.000; tables below, with the CG slices):\n\n**4. CG at leading order [numeric].** All HW CG data are read from the overlap alone, for both reps (6/6 and 10/10), errors and spreads ∝ ε (ratio 4.00 between 1e-6 and 4e-6), second-order Richardson limits overlap vs chain agree to 1e-16 … 1e-20 (or exactly for the 1-dim slices of the first irreps), and the chain limits reproduce the earlier reference numbers (46.67453891, 10.92853892, −5118.538314, 184.3305612, −238.5587523; [3,1,0]: 46.6745, −36.8838, −1325.402, −334.332):\n\n**[2,1,0]: K/S** (main family: exponents and max|K/S| at ε = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6; other families: max|K/S| at ε = 1e-6)\n\n| irrep | copy | S eps-exp | K eps-exp | max abs(K/S), main, 1e-6 / 2e-6 / 4e-6 | fixed w′ | inf2 (w₂=w₂′=∞) | inf1 (w₂′=∞) | common1 (w₁′=w₁) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [4,2,0] | 1 | -2.000, -2.000 | K=0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| [4,1,1] | 1 | -3.000, -3.000 | -2.000, -2.000 | 4.25e-7 / 8.5e-7 / 1.7e-6 | 6.02e-6 | 2.22e-6 | 2.89e-5 | 2.33e-7 |\n| [3,3,0] | 1 | -3.000, -3.000 | -2.000, -2.000 | 2.1e-6 / 4.21e-6 / 8.42e-6 | 6.52e-7 | 2.1e-6 | 2.1e-6 | not read |\n| [3,2,1] | 1 | -4.000, -4.000 | -3.000, -3.000 | 1.5e-5 / 3.01e-5 / 6.01e-5 | 6.03e-7 | 2.72e-6 | 2.39e-6 | not read |\n| [3,2,1] | 2 | -4.000, -4.000 | -3.000, -3.000 | 8.05e-6 / 1.61e-5 / 3.22e-5 | 1.36e-6 | 1.e-5 | 3.04e-6 | not read |\n| [2,2,2] | 1 | -6.000, -6.000 | -5.000, -5.000 | 2.57e-6 / 5.14e-6 / 1.03e-5 | 9.91e-7 | 2.27e-6 | 3.77e-6 | not read |\n\n**[2,1,0]: CG slices** (main family; error and spread are maxima over the grid)\n\n| irrep | copy | slice dim | spread (1e-6, 4e-6) | error vs chain at 1e-6 / 2e-6 / 4e-6 | Richardson: overlap vs chain | chain Richardson limit of the slice |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [4,2,0] | 1 | 1 | < 1e-192, < 1e-192 | < 1e-192 / < 1e-192 / < 1e-192 | < 1e-191 | 2.60946745562 |\n| [4,1,1] | 1 | 1 | 4.68e-7, 1.87e-6 | 4.25e-7 / 8.5e-7 / 1.7e-6 | < 1e-184 | 46.6745389114 |\n| [3,3,0] | 1 | 1 | 1.61e-6, 6.44e-6 | 2.1e-6 / 4.21e-6 / 8.42e-6 | < 1e-184 | 10.9285389167 |\n| [3,2,1] | 1 | 2 | 5.62e-5, 2.25e-4 | 5.46e-5 / 1.09e-4 / 2.19e-4 | 1.23e-18 | (248.327054711, -21.3321644927) |\n| [3,2,1] | 2 | 2 | 6.09e-5, 2.43e-4 | 6.76e-5 / 1.35e-4 / 2.7e-4 | 7.34e-18 | (11.3988399453, -83.3191974257) |\n| [2,2,2] | 1 | 1 | 2.5e-6, 9.98e-6 | 2.57e-6 / 5.14e-6 / 1.03e-5 | 1.51e-19 | -5118.53831440 |\n\n**[3,1,0]: K/S** (main family: exponents and max|K/S| at ε = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6; other families: max|K/S| at ε = 1e-6)\n\n| irrep | copy | S eps-exp | K eps-exp | max abs(K/S), main, 1e-6 / 2e-6 / 4e-6 | fixed w′ | inf2 (w₂=w₂′=∞) | inf1 (w₂′=∞) | common1 (w₁′=w₁) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [6,2,0] | 1 | -2.000, -2.000 | K=0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| [6,1,1] | 1 | -3.000, -3.000 | -2.000, -2.000 | 4.25e-7 / 8.5e-7 / 1.7e-6 | 6.02e-6 | 2.22e-6 | 2.89e-5 | 2.33e-7 |\n| [5,3,0] | 1 | -3.000, -3.000 | -2.000, -2.000 | 3.12e-7 / 6.24e-7 / 1.25e-6 | 9.66e-8 | 3.12e-7 | 3.12e-7 | not read |\n| [5,2,1] | 1 | -4.000, -4.000 | -3.000, -3.000 | 5.65e-7 / 1.13e-6 / 2.26e-6 | 8.68e-7 | 3.23e-6 | 1.96e-5 | not read |\n| [5,2,1] | 2 | -4.000, -4.000 | -3.000, -3.000 | 2.e-5 / 4.e-5 / 8.01e-5 | 2.1e-6 | 5.2e-6 | 3.51e-6 | not read |\n| [4,4,0] | 1 | -4.000, -4.000 | -3.000, -3.000 | 4.21e-6 / 8.42e-6 / 1.68e-5 | 1.3e-6 | 4.21e-6 | 4.21e-6 | not read |\n| [4,3,1] | 1 | -5.000, -5.000 | -4.000, -4.000 | 3.69e-6 / 7.38e-6 / 1.48e-5 | 1.06e-6 | 1.08e-6 | 3.2e-6 | not read |\n| [4,3,1] | 2 | -5.000, -5.000 | -4.000, -4.000 | 1.09e-5 / 2.18e-5 / 4.36e-5 | 1.7e-6 | 1.01e-5 | 3.56e-6 | not read |\n| [4,2,2] | 1 | -6.000, -6.000 | -5.000, -5.000 | 4.51e-6 / 9.02e-6 / 1.8e-5 | 2.08e-6 | 3.1e-6 | 2.96e-6 | not read |\n| [3,3,2] | 1 | -7.000, -7.000 | -6.000, -5.997 | 4.44e-6 / 8.88e-6 / 1.78e-5 | 1.39e-6 | 3.99e-6 | 6.93e-6 | not read |\n\n**[3,1,0]: CG slices** (main family; error and spread are maxima over the grid)\n\n| irrep | copy | slice dim | spread (1e-6, 4e-6) | error vs chain at 1e-6 / 2e-6 / 4e-6 | Richardson: overlap vs chain | chain Richardson limit of the slice |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [6,2,0] | 1 | 1 | < 1e-191, < 1e-192 | < 1e-191 / < 1e-192 / < 1e-192 | < 1e-191 | 2.60946745562 |\n| [6,1,1] | 1 | 1 | 4.68e-7, 1.87e-6 | 4.25e-7 / 8.5e-7 / 1.7e-6 | < 1e-184 | 46.6745389114 |\n| [5,3,0] | 1 | 1 | 2.38e-7, 9.54e-7 | 3.12e-7 / 6.24e-7 / 1.25e-6 | < 1e-183 | -36.8838188439 |\n| [5,2,1] | 1 | 2 | 1.02e-5, 4.07e-5 | 1.17e-5 / 2.33e-5 / 4.66e-5 | 1.44e-19 | (-835.970434496, 43.3173128073) |\n| [5,2,1] | 2 | 2 | 3.29e-5, 1.32e-4 | 3.78e-5 / 7.55e-5 / 1.51e-4 | 9.67e-19 | (22.7423320599, -47.4770351603) |\n| [4,4,0] | 1 | 1 | 3.22e-6, 1.29e-5 | 4.21e-6 / 8.42e-6 / 1.68e-5 | 1.66e-19 | -115.853020728 |\n| [4,3,1] | 1 | 2 | 1.2e-4, 4.78e-4 | 1.21e-4 / 2.43e-4 / 4.86e-4 | 3.71e-19 | (-3129.70920645, 247.139873999) |\n| [4,3,1] | 2 | 2 | 7.24e-5, 2.9e-4 | 7.94e-5 / 1.59e-4 / 3.18e-4 | 4.52e-17 | (-65.0505836460, 570.310701774) |\n| [4,2,2] | 1 | 2 | 5.53e-6, 2.21e-5 | 6.4e-6 / 1.28e-5 / 2.56e-5 | 3.31e-18 | (4647.35409165, -1549.11803055) |\n| [3,3,2] | 1 | 1 | 4.26e-6, 1.71e-5 | 4.44e-6 / 8.88e-6 / 1.78e-5 | 6.98e-19 | 23369.8056448 |\n\n**5. Task 5 (for the Q side).** The vacuum Q's of w and w′, the dual Q's, the four overlaps and their ε-exponents are tabulated above (Task 5 result). ⟨Ω_w⊗Ω_w|Ψ⟩ = c_w det₆/Ψ_Q state-independently (3e-116 / 6e-77); the mixed overlaps are the Stage C targets and carry the slice exponents (−2 top, −3, −4, … −7).\n\n**6. Surprises and consequences.**\n1. **No untwisting of w′ is needed**, and the pinned/fixed w′ controls are as clean as the full regime (K/S = O(ε), all CG data): the old degeneration came from slaving the second vacuum to the first (resolvent, y pinned); with two independent vacua g′ = (b−b_{w′})−(a−a_{w′})c has no pinned denominator. The family needs only w₁′ ≠ w₁.\n2. **The cheap sub-family w₂ = w₂′ = ∞ (Stage B block counts 8/14) is CG-complete** at finite twist, at ε⁰ in the regime and in K/S and CG extraction (the HANDOFF reading \"no cheap AND CG-complete two-vacuum family\" is therefore contradicted at the chain level; the expectation \"global rotation, top irrep only\" holds only for w₁′ = w₁). Only two direction parameters (ω₁, ω₁′) remain; the ε⁰ data are then a surface in (a′₀,g′₀,c′₀)-space but per-weight ranks are still full. What remains open is the Q side: that the (∞,∞) overlap is the cheap bracket expression (Stage C), and the O(ε) layer.\n3. Two spec statements were corrected: the frame tie holds up to the scalar κ (Task 0), and the eigen-covector twist is G′(w), not diag(w).\n4. Undo accuracy 1e-157 … 1e-192 ([3,3,2] 1e-149) at 200 digits; the Q-determinant identities are limited by the ~100-digit precision of the Q's.\n\n**Timings (s), [2,1,0] / [3,1,0]:** setup 0.05/0.07, 0.26/1.6, 0.09/0.22, 0.03/0.12; Task 0 0.16/0.86; branches (all HW-sector states at one ε) 1.5/5.2; Task 1 0.15/0.21; Task 1b 0.03/0.05; Task 2 0.24/0.44; Task 3 (222 point-evaluations over all families, every branch) 4.9/14; Task 4 0.4/0.8; Task 5 0.75/2.1. Whole notebook ≈ 8 s / 26 s.",
